        "attrs": {
         "hex": "A64D79"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Crescendo/Decrescendo: systolic murmur assoc. w stenotic aortic valve. When Lt ventricle squeezes, blood is forced through stenotic aortic valve =murmur.  As ventricle squeezes, P goes up, peaks & goes back down as ventricle relaxes. So, murmur ↑  intensity until P ventricle peaks, then murmur ↓ as ventricle relaxes. called crescendo/decrescendo. starts @ S1 & ends @ S2. takes few millisec to build enough P in ventricle to start murmur it = midsystolic.  "
     }
    ]
   },
