      ],
      "text": "Holosystolic: cont. systolic murmur of mitral valve regurg (pansystolic)  As Lt ventricle squeezes, it pushes blood retrograde into Lt atrium =murmur. ventricular P will continue > atrial P throughout systole so sound over mitral valve stays same. murmur starts @ S1 & ends @ S2, when mitral/tricuspid valve completely opens for start of systole. time murmur starts @ beginning systole b/c ⍉ P gradient to overcome like in aortic stenosis.  "
